{
  "id": "32174_uwaru",
  "headword": "{植|う}わる",
  "reading": "うわる",
  "romaji": "uwaru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to be planted",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to be planted (in the ground)",
      "explanation": "Of a plant, to be planted somewhere and growing there. The intransitive partner of {植|う}える, used almost always as {植|う}わっている to say what is planted where."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "32174_uwaru_ex1",
      "japanese": "⟦{庭|にわ}→庭：02239_niwa⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{桜|さくら}→桜：02212_sakura⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{植|う}わって⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧。",
      "english": "A cherry tree is planted in the garden.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": true,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "32174_uwaru_ex2",
      "japanese": "⟦{道|みち}→道：00505_michi⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{両側|りょうがわ}→両側：28877_ryougawa⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{松|まつ}→松：02256_matsu⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{植|う}わって⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧。",
      "english": "Pine trees are planted along both sides of the road.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": true,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "32174_uwaru_ex3",
      "japanese": "⟦{鉢|はち}→鉢：29581_hachi⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{植|う}わったまま⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{花|はな}→花：00523_hana⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧、⟦{庭|にわ}→庭：02239_niwa⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{植|う}え{替|か}えた→植え替える：17856_uekaeru⟧。",
      "english": "I moved the flowers that were still in their pot into the garden.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": true,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive. The transitive partner is ⟦{植|う}える→植える：01210_ueru⟧ (to plant): ⟦{木|き}→木：00524_ki⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{植|う}える→植える：01210_ueru⟧ → ⟦{木|き}→木：00524_ki⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{植|う}わる.\n\nASPECT (ている):\nAlmost always {植|う}わって⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧, describing the resulting state: something is planted there. The plain form {植|う}わる is rare.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{植|う}えてある→植える：01210_ueru⟧: has been planted — stresses that someone planted it\n- ⟦{生|は}えている→生える：02392_haeru⟧: is growing — for plants that grew by themselves, and for hair",
